    "body": "So `visibility: hidden` doesn't affect HTML's definition of [being rendered](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#being-rendered) at all since `visibility: hidden` doesn't change whether the element has any CSS layout boxes.\r\n\r\nI think trying to solve this using something like \"at least one of its descendants is being rendered\" will have unintended side effects, in terms of interactions with other mechanisms that can render content from a different subtree (whether things like `svg:use` reaching in to content or things like `datalist`).  I'd like to define something here that only affects `display: contents` (and that we could add to later if there's something else that works similarly) and doesn't use wording that may pick up other content-hiding mechanisms that work in very different ways.",
    "created_at": "2024-01-10T18:02:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-10T18:02:13Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9425#discussion_r1447742964",
